SUMMARY:Civic Meetup #567: Insights from the Tracking (In)justice Project
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T210000
UID:90cde2f17a37cdd15a0a8d818e282304@guild.host
DESCRIPTION:Topic: Insights from the Tracking (In)justice Project\n\nLast 
 year\, 61 people died in interactions with the police or in incarceration 
 facilities across the country. Historically\, we lacked means for systemat
 ically tracking even basic details of the circumstances around these death
 s\, including rudimentary demographic information (who was killed?)\, geog
 raphic (where were they killed?)\, as well as investigative outcomes (were
  any officials held responsible?)\, and journalistic coverage (has there b
 een any reporting about this)? With a team of researchers spanning Carleto
 n\, McGill\, Queens\, UofT\, and UBC\, we are developing the Tracking (In)
 Justice project to systematically and transparently catalogue the circumst
 ances around these deaths\, drawing on a mix of sources from government re
 leases\, news reporting\, and meticulous case-by-case fact checking\, trac
 king these critical details from 2000 onwards.\n\n‎\n\nSpeaker: Farhan S
 amir (he/him) (in-person)\n\nFarhan Samir is a Natural Sciences and Engine
 ering Research Council (NSERC) Postdoctoral Fellow in the Computer Science
  department at the University of Toronto. He earned his PhD at the Univers
 ity of British Columbia\, where his work was supported by an NSERC Doctora
 l Fellowship\, a UBC Public Scholars Initiative award\, and the 2024-25 UB
 C Department of Statistics Award in Data Science. He was formerly a resear
 cher at NVIDIA\, Amazon Science\, and the Allen Institute for AI.\n\n‎\n
 \nAgenda:\n\n7:00-7:20 Welcome and Introductions\n\n7:20-7:50 Presentation
  and Q\\&A/discussion\n\n7:50-9:00 Breakout groups\n\n‎\n\nCode of Condu
 ct: https://civictech.ca/about-us\n\n‎\n\nCheck in with us on the Civic 
 Tech Toronto Slack: https://link.civictech.ca/chat\n\n‎\n\nAbout Us:\n\n
 Our weekly civic meetups bring together Torontonians (designers\, coders\,
  urban planners\, government staff\, mappers\, policy-makers\, students\, 
 communications strategists\, community organizers\, and more) who share an
  interest in making Toronto more responsive\, prosperous\, sustainable\, a
 nd equitable through design\, tech\, and data.\n\nCome and be part of it!\
 n\nFor more info: https://civictech.ca\n\n\\--\n\nSuggest a Speaker:&#x20\
 ;\n\nInterested in speaking at a future event\, or know someone who'd be a
  great speaker? We'd love to hear from you: https://link.civictech.ca/spea
 ker-suggestions\n\nSuggest a Venue:&#x20\;\n\nHave a space that could host
  up to 80 civic-minded folks for an evening? Consider recommending your ve
 nue: https://link.civictech.ca/venue-suggestions\n
LOCATION:Online: https://link.civictech.ca/zoom / Metro Hall
